Name the key directory at run time, and fail instead of spinning

shmget() with a key records the key as a symbolic link in a directory
that was compiled in (_PATH_TMP). An app's writable directories are
named after its package, so any compiled-in directory is right for one
package only: iCode's build named another package's cache, which this
app cannot write. When symlink() failed for that reason, the loop that
takes ownership of the key ran again forever, holding the mutex.

The directory now comes from PROOT_TMP_DIR, which iCode sets for PRoot
to the running app's own temporary directory, and a symlink() failure
other than EEXIST returns -1 with its errno. Reached only through
PRoot's --sysvipc extension, which iCode does not enable today.

Upstream: termux/libandroid-shmem 7f0bd7e. Applied by
app/src/main/cpp/CMakeLists.txt.

--- a/shmem.c
+++ b/shmem.c
@@ -23,7 +23,14 @@
 #include "shm.h"
 
 #define DBG(...) __android_log_print(ANDROID_LOG_INFO, "shmem", __VA_ARGS__)
-#define ASHV_KEY_SYMLINK_PATH _PATH_TMP "ashv_key_%d"
+// The running app's own temporary directory, named at run time: iCode sets
+// PROOT_TMP_DIR for PRoot. A directory compiled in names one package only,
+// and another package's directory cannot be written.
+static const char *ashv_key_dir(void)
+{
+	const char *dir = getenv("PROOT_TMP_DIR");
+	return dir != NULL && dir[0] != '\0' ? dir : "/data/local/tmp";
+}
 #define ANDROID_SHMEM_SOCKNAME "/dev/shm/%08x"
 #define ROUND_UP(N, S) ((((N) + (S) - 1) / (S)) * (S))
 
@@ -349,7 +356,7 @@
